# Agent Chat Surfaces (Common Component)

Every client surface that talks to a chat/agent thread (Agent Home, interviews, ADR/PRD/design-doc
assistants, standups, dev sessions, calendar assistant, etc.) MUST build on the shared hook
`useAgentChatSession` (`src/client/hooks/useAgentChatSession.ts`).

Behind `useAgentChatSession`, governed chat areas run on the shared client chat harness runtime
(`src/client/chatHarness/`). The runtime opens one WebSocket per thread with automatic reconnect
and event replay, falls back to HTTP commands when needed, maintains a server-authoritative store,
and records client timing telemetry. Threads without a harness area keep the HTTP send/cancel/retry
path.

Do **not** hand-roll agent transport with raw `fetch`, custom sockets, or `useEffect` polling.
Reuse the common hook so send, steer, summarize, cancel, retry, awaiting-response tracking,
preparation state, and streaming flags stay consistent across every surface.

## Use the hook's contract

- **Options**: `harnessArea`, `locked`, `beforeSend` / `afterSend`, `sendEndpoint` /
  `cancelEndpoint`, `visibleMessageFilter`, `enablePreparationState`, `initialMessages` /
  `initialStatus`.
- **Actions**: `send(text, { attachments, model })`, `steer(text)`, `summarize()`, `retryLast()`,
  `retryFailedRun()`, `cancel()`.
- **Derived flags** (drive UI, do not recompute): `isInteractionBusy`, `isRunning`, `isSending`,
  `isAwaitingAgentResponse`, `isPreparing`, `hasPreparationError`, `canWrite`.
- **Stream state**: `visibleMessages`, `streamingText`, `thinkingText`, `toolProgress`,
  `phaseEvents`, `runHealth`, `progressLabel`, `connectionState`, `pendingCommands`,
  `lastReceipt`, `activity`, `summaryNotice`.

## Three user-facing archetypes (one chat UX inside)

Keep surfaces distinct by **workspace and permissions**, never by forked chat mechanics. Every surface fits one of three archetypes, all rendered inside `AgentHarnessPanel` with the exact same composer, streaming, steer, stop, and proposal UX:

1. **Open Chat / Workspace** (*Agent Home, Brainstorm*) — free-form exploration with optional artifact canvas and promote/handoff tools.
2. **Guided Workflows** (*Interviews, ADR Interviews, Standup, Build Intake*) — workflow header/progress bar, structured Q&A option cards, and a clear finish line.
3. **Contextual Side-Panel Copilots** (*PRD, Design Doc, Calendar, QA Lab, CAB Release, Ask Apex*) — docked beside an existing record, automatically grounded in that record, with propose-and-apply write tools.

## `AgentHarnessPanel` and its five area slots

Render governed chat areas inside `AgentHarnessPanel`
(`src/client/components/agentChat/AgentHarnessPanel.tsx`), wired to `useAgentChatSession`. Add
area-specific UI through its five slots rather than duplicating the panel shell or transcript:

- `header` — area title, status badges, or top-bar actions.
- `sidePanel` — optional side drawer or inspector beside the conversation.
- `composerAccessory` — controls near the composer (model picker, mode/skill selector, context
  attachments).
- `messageActions` — per-message controls (ratings, copy, follow-up actions).
- `proposal` — proposed edits or domain writes; writes wait for explicit user confirmation and are
  never auto-approved.

Preserve each area's existing `data-testid` values by passing `testIdPrefix` or explicit `testIds`
so existing tests keep matching.

## Single live progress, thought process, and failure UX

Do not fork or duplicate live status indicators, thought-process drawers, or failure retry bars
inside area components:

- **Default transcript first**: prefer `AgentHarnessPanel`'s built-in transcript. Only use
  `renderTranscript` when an area needs domain-specific message widgets (such as interview Q&A
  choice cards, standup grouping, or the Brainstorm turn ledger).
- **Live agent work**: every governed area must render `liveWorkBox` (`AgentLiveWorkBox`) from
  `AgentHarnessPanel` while a turn is running or retrying — do **not** add bespoke typing-dot
  spinners or a standalone `<AgentRetryBanner>` alongside it.
- **Single run-status text component**: render phase/waiting labels through `AgentRunStatusText`
  (`src/client/components/agentChat/AgentRunStatusText.tsx`) and `friendlyChatProgressLabel` — never
  hardcode raw infrastructure strings like `"Queued"` or `"Dispatched"` in area components.
- **Reconnect / retry clearing**: the harness event reducer (`src/client/chatHarness/reducers/eventReducer.ts`) clears `isRetrying` and
  `retryReason` on any active progress event (`phase`, `thinking`, `tool_call`, `tool_status`,
  `token`, `message`, `done`). Do not keep a separate client-side reconnecting flag.
- **Completed thought process**: render `AgentThoughtProcess` above completed agent replies when
  `activity?.length || activityUnavailable` is present so users get the same collapsible
  `Thought process · N steps` drawer in every governed area.
- **Single failure surface**: render one failure/retry control per failed turn — never stack a
  legacy `Error:` system-message retry bar above `AgentHarnessPanel`'s `messageFailure` card.

## Composer, Steer, and Summarize

Governed surfaces keep one consistent composer experience and expose `steer` and `summarize` directly from `useAgentChatSession`:

- **Keep the composer unlocked while running** on every governed surface (`do not` pass `isRunning`
  into `composer.disabled`). While running, `AgentComposer` shows the standard send icon for
  mid-turn follow-ups (`steer`) beside the Stop button, with placeholder `"Send a follow-up while the agent works…"`.
- Call `steer(text)` to send mid-turn guidance while a run is active, and display command status
  from `lastReceipt`.
- `Summarize` is opt-in (`composer.showSummarize === true`) and hidden by default. When opted in,
  call `summarize()` and display status from `summaryNotice`.
- The server owns the 5-steer cap and the summary lifecycle. Do not count steers or track summary
  state independently in client components.
- Read-only users (`canWrite: false`) cannot send, steer, summarize, cancel, or rate. Disable or
  hide those controls when `canWrite` is `false`.
- **No new bespoke transport endpoints**: `sendEndpoint`, `cancelEndpoint`, and `retryEndpoint`
  overrides exist only for legacy migrations (e.g. Brainstorm). New areas must use the shared
  harness command channel paired with server `areaHooks` (`src/server/services/chatHarness/areaHooks.ts`).

## Sanctioned exception to the TanStack Query rule

`react-coding-standards.mdc` requires server/async state to go through TanStack Query and forbids
`fetch` in effects. Agent chat is the **one sanctioned exception**: live WebSocket streaming,
reconnect/replay, and imperative commands live inside `src/client/chatHarness/` and
`useAgentChatSession`. Route chat surfaces through `useAgentChatSession` instead of
`useQuery`/`useMutation` — do not re-implement the transport elsewhere.

## Adding a new chat area

Follow `.cursor/rules/chat-harness.mdc` on the server side too: declare an area profile in
`src/server/services/chatHarness/areaProfiles.ts` and route every Cursor SDK call through
`src/server/services/cursorSdkAdapter/`.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — reuse useAgentChatSession and AgentHarnessPanel with an area profile
const session = useAgentChatSession(threadId, {
  harnessArea: 'myArea',
  enablePreparationState: true,
  beforeSend: async () => { /* confirm / sync token */ },
});

<AgentHarnessPanel
  session={session}
  testIdPrefix="my-area-chat"
  slots={{
    header: <MyAreaHeader />,
    composerAccessory: <MyModelPicker />,
    proposal: <MyConfirmationCard />,
  }}
/>;

// ❌ BAD — new chat area skips the area profile, AgentHarnessPanel, and useAgentChatSession
const socket = new WebSocket(`/api/custom-chat/${threadId}`);
await fetch(`/api/custom-chat/${threadId}/messages`, { method: 'POST', ... });
return <CustomBespokeChatPanel messages={localMessages} />;
```

If `useAgentChatSession` or `AgentHarnessPanel` lacks a capability, extend the shared hook or
panel rather than forking chat logic into a feature component.
